Sam: Yes, the forecast says it will reach our city after midnight.
Lily: We should buy enough water and some food that doesn''t need cooking.
Sam: Good idea. I''ll also buy some batteries in case the power goes off.
Lily: Don''t forget to bring the plants inside and close all the windows.
Sam: Right. My dad said we should tape the big windows so the glass won''t break.
Lily: And we must stay indoors once it starts. The streets won''t be safe.
Sam: Agreed. Let''s keep the radio on for the latest announcements.', 'Lily 告诉 Sam 今晚有强台风;预报说午夜后到城;两人决定买足够的水和免煮食物、买电池以防停电;把植物搬进屋、关好窗;Sam 的爸爸说要给大窗户贴胶带以防玻璃碎;台风一来就待在室内、开着收音机听最新公告。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When will the typhoon reach the city?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["After midnight.","Early in the morning.","At noon.","Next week."]},{"q":"Why does Sam want to buy batteries?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To sell them later.","In case the power goes off.","To give them to Lily.","Because they are cheap."]},{"q":"What does Sam''s dad suggest doing to the big windows?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Taping them so the glass won''t break.","Painting them white.","Opening them wide.","Removing them completely."]},{"q":"What must they do once the typhoon starts?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Walk in the streets.","Stay indoors.","Drive to the beach.","Visit their neighbours."]},{"q":"How will they get the latest news?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["By reading old newspapers.","By calling the school.","By keeping the radio on.","By looking at the stars."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Most tsunamis are caused by a strong earthquake under the ocean floor.
When the sea floor suddenly moves, it pushes a huge amount of water upward.
This water travels across the ocean as fast as a plane, but in deep water the waves are still quite low.
Only when the waves reach shallow water near the coast do they grow into giant walls of water, so people must move to high ground as soon as a warning is given.', '海啸是海上最危险的事件之一;大多数海啸由海底强烈地震引起;海底突然移动时,会把大量海水向上推;这股水以飞机般的速度横越大洋,但在深水区浪还很低;只有当波浪到达海岸边的浅水区才会长成巨墙般的水墙,所以一旦发出警报,人们必须立刻转移到高处。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What causes most tsunamis?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Heavy rain on the beach.","Wind from the mountains.","A long drought.","A strong earthquake under the ocean floor."]},{"q":"How fast does the water travel across the ocean?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["As fast as a plane.","As slow as a person walking.","Slower than a boat.","It does not move at all."]},{"q":"In deep water, what are the waves like?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They are already giant walls.","They are still quite low.","They stop completely.","They turn into ice."]},{"q":"When do the waves grow into giant walls of water?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["When the wind stops.","When the sun rises.","When they reach shallow water near the coast.","When the rain begins."]},{"q":"What must people do when a warning is given?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Run towards the sea.","Wait on the beach.","Go back to sleep.","Move to high ground at once."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Mr Li: It happened so fast. The ground shook, and our house came down in seconds.
Anna: That sounds terrible. How did you and your family escape?
Mr Li: We were lucky. A rescue team pulled us out from under the broken walls.
Anna: How long did you have to wait before help came?
Mr Li: About two days, but it felt like months in the dark.
Anna: What kept you going during that time?
Mr Li: My wife kept saying that as long as we were together, there was still hope.
Anna: And how is life now?
Mr Li: Now we are rebuilding our home, and many kind strangers have helped us.', '记者 Anna 采访地震幸存者李先生;地震发生极快,房子几秒就塌了;一支救援队把全家从断墙下救出;他们等了约两天才等到救援,黑暗中却觉得像几个月;支撑他的是妻子常说的——只要一家人在一起就还有希望;如今他们正在重建家园,许多好心的陌生人也帮助了他们。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What happened to Mr Li''s house?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It came down in seconds.","It was only slightly damaged.","It was moved to a new street.","It stayed completely safe."]},{"q":"How did the family escape?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They climbed out by themselves.","A rescue team pulled them out.","A helicopter lifted the house.","They were never trapped."]},{"q":"How long did they wait for help?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only a few minutes.","Several months.","About two days.","Almost a year."]},{"q":"What did his wife keep saying?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They should give up.","Help would never come.","It was nobody''s fault.","As long as they were together, there was still hope."]},{"q":"What is the family doing now?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Rebuilding their home.","Leaving the country.","Selling their land.","Living in the dark."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Long ago, they watched the clouds, the wind and even the behaviour of animals.
Today, satellites high above the Earth send back pictures of storms while they are still far out at sea.
Computers then use this data to work out where a storm will go and how strong it will be.
Thanks to these tools, scientists can now forecast dangerous weather far more precisely, and a warning sent out in time can save thousands of lives.', '几千年来人们一直试图预测天气;很久以前,他们靠观察云、风,甚至动物的行为;如今,高悬地球上空的卫星在风暴还远在海上时就传回它们的图像;计算机再用这些数据算出风暴的去向和强度;借助这些工具,科学家如今能更精确地预报危险天气,而及时发出的警报能挽救成千上万的生命。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How did people predict the weather long ago?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["By using satellites.","By watching clouds, wind and animals.","By reading computer data.","By asking scientists."]},{"q":"What do satellites send back?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Boxes of food.","Weather reports on paper.","Pictures of storms far out at sea.","Phone numbers."]},{"q":"What do computers use the satellite data for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To play music.","To draw maps of the past.","To count the stars.","To work out where a storm will go and how strong it will be."]},{"q":"What can scientists do better now than before?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Forecast dangerous weather more precisely.","Stop storms completely.","Control the wind.","Make the rain warmer."]},{"q":"What can a warning sent out in time do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Make storms stronger.","Save thousands of lives.","Cost a lot of money.","Hide the clouds."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U6', 'fltrp');
Ms Green: Good afternoon. I''m afraid it will continue for at least three more days.
Mr Brown: That''s worrying. The temperature has already reached forty degrees here.
Ms Green: Yes, it''s exceptionally hot. Please drink plenty of water and stay out of the sun.
Mr Brown: My grandmother feels dizzy. Is there anything I can do to help her?
Ms Green: Keep her in a cool room and give her cool water. If she gets worse, call a doctor.
Mr Brown: Thank you. Will there be any rain soon?
Ms Green: Some rain is expected at the weekend, which should make things cooler.', 'Brown 先生致电气象站,询问热浪还会持续多久;Green 女士说至少还有三天;当地气温已达四十度;她提醒多喝水、避开阳光;Brown 的祖母头晕,Green 建议让老人待在凉爽房间、喝凉水,若加重就叫医生;周末预计有雨,天气会转凉。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why is Mr Brown calling the weather station?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To report a flood.","To ask about a typhoon.","To check how long the heatwave will last.","To buy a thermometer."]},{"q":"How much longer will the heatwave last?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only a few hours.","About a month.","It has already ended.","At least three more days."]},{"q":"What does Ms Green advise Mr Brown to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Drink plenty of water and stay out of the sun.","Go for a long walk at noon.","Turn off all the lights.","Drive to the mountains."]},{"q":"What should he do for his grandmother?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Take her out into the sun.","Keep her in a cool room and give her cool water.","Give her hot soup.","Let her sleep on the roof."]},{"q":"When is some rain expected?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Tonight.","In three months.","At the weekend.","Never this year."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U6', 'fltrp');
All around the world, people who have lost almost everything still find the strength to start again.
Neighbours share food and shelter, strangers send money and clothes, and rescue teams travel from faraway countries to help.
Little by little, broken towns come back to life, and new homes rise where old ones once stood.
A disaster shows us how powerful nature can be, but it also shows that human kindness and hope can shine even in the darkest of times.', '灾难袭来时,它能夺走我们的家园,却夺不走我们的勇气;世界各地,失去几乎一切的人仍能找到重新开始的力量;邻里分享食物与庇护,陌生人寄来钱物,救援队从遥远的国度赶来相助;一点一点地,破碎的城镇重新焕发生机,新家在旧址上拔地而起;灾难让我们看到自然的强大,也让我们看到——人间的善意与希望,即使在最黑暗的时刻也能闪光。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What can a disaster NOT take away, according to the speaker?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Our homes.","Our furniture.","Our streets.","Our courage."]},{"q":"What do neighbours share?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Food and shelter.","Cars and boats.","Phones and games.","Maps and books."]},{"q":"Where do the rescue teams travel from?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The same street.","Faraway countries.","Under the sea.","Outer space."]},{"q":"What happens to broken towns little by little?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They are forgotten forever.","They sink into the sea.","They come back to life.","They stay empty."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say can shine in the darkest times?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Bright city lights.","The hot summer sun.","Expensive machines.","Human kindness and hope."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U6', 'fltrp');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE publisher='fltrp' AND volume='required3' AND unit='U6';

The rainy season has arrived, and floods are a real threat. Here is how to stay safe.

Before a flood: Remember to store sufficient food, clean water and batteries. It''s important to move valuable things to a higher floor.

During a flood: Move to high ground immediately and listen to the latest warnings. Never walk or drive through fast-moving water, and do not drink the flood water; otherwise you may get sick.

Being well prepared is the best way to keep your family safe. Stay calm, stay safe!', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["Remember to store sufficient food, clean water and batteries.","Move to high ground immediately and listen to the latest warnings.","Never walk or drive through fast-moving water.","Being well prepared is the best way to keep your family safe."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"It''s important moving valuables higher.","correct":"It''s important to move valuables higher.","note":"It''s important to do sth,后接不定式。"},{"wrong":"Don''t drink the flood water, otherwise you will sick.","correct":"Don''t drink the flood water; otherwise you will get sick.","note":"sick 是形容词,要用 get/be sick;otherwise 前用分号或句号。"},{"wrong":"When flooded, move to high ground are important.","correct":"When flooded, moving to high ground is important.","note":"动名词短语作主语视为单数,谓语用 is。"}]'::jsonb, '【洪水安全指南结构】
标题 Flood Safety Guidelines
Before a flood: Remember to … / It''s important to …
During a flood: Move to high ground immediately … Never …
结尾鼓励: Being well prepared is the best way to stay safe.', 2, 'required3', 'U6', 'fltrp');

